// TYPOGRAPHY ONLY, and now a single call site: the auction side rail, where it
// is a paragraph that may take the height it needs.
//
// It rendered in the 70px bid bar too until 2026-09-02, and the pair is worth
// remembering if anyone proposes putting it back. The sentence names every team
// still to answer, so it has no natural upper length; in the bar it therefore
// had to be bounded on both axes, and a flex shorthand written HERE resolves
// against whichever axis the PARENT happens to run -- the one basis that
// bounded the bar's width made the rail's copy a 240px-tall block for a single
// sentence. Bounded and clamped instead, the bar copy was simply cut off, which
// is what retired that call site.
.auction-settlement-status
  margin-right 10px
  padding 4px 8px
  font-size 12px
  line-height 1.3
  // Was `var(--text-color-secondary)`, a custom property declared in no
  // stylesheet in this repo -- so the declaration was invalid at computed-value
  // time and dropped entirely, and this text had never once rendered in a
  // secondary colour. It greps clean and reads as correct CSS, which is what
  // makes it survive review. This app styles from the stylus tokens in
  // `app/styles/variables.styl`; a CSS custom property here is the exception
  // and has to be declared somewhere before it means anything. The literal
  // below is the same secondary-text value the auction election control uses.
  color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6)
